  "skills": [
    "logic.de-morgan"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "Same drawer, same NAND chips, but now the alarm should sound if either sensor trips: OR. De Morgan’s law says NOT A NAND NOT B is A OR B. Gates 1 and 2 already invert each input.",
    "goal": "Wire the two inverted inputs (pins 3 and 6) into gate 3 (pins 9 and 10) so LED1 = SA OR SB.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "74HC00 · quad NAND",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Gate 1",
          "NOT SA → pin 3 (column 12)"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 2",
          "NOT SB → pin 6 (column 15)"
        ],
        [
          "Gate 3",
          "pins 9, 10 → 8 (bottom row)"
        ],
        [
          "Pins 9, 10",
          "columns 15, 14 (row f)"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Pins 8–14 come back along row f, right to left: pin 8 is column 16, pin 9 column 15, pin 10 column 14. Bottom-half holes (g–j) reach them.",
    "Gate 3 needs NOT SA and NOT SB: pin 3 (top of column 12) to pin 9 (bottom of column 15), and pin 6 (top of column 15) to pin 10 (bottom of column 14).",
    "Wires: column 12 top → column 15 bottom, and column 15 top → column 14 bottom. NAND(NOT A, NOT B) = A OR B."
  ],
